{
  "info": {
    "name": "KairoX \u00b7 Material",
    "description": "Lots, stock, receiving (with per-hide leather sheets), the supplier directory, and the style's material recipe.\n\nSETUP\n  1. Import the whole folder and SELECT the KairoX environment\n     (top-right). That is what shares one token across every\n     collection \u2014 a collection variable is visible only to the\n     collection that set it.\n  2. Run `user` \u2192 Login. Its test script stores `access_token` for\n     you; there is nothing to copy and paste.\n  3. Every request here inherits bearer auth from that token.\n\n`base_url` defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000.\n\nOptional query params are present but DISABLED, so each request runs\nas-is. File uploads are real form-data rows \u2014 click Select Files on\nthe `file` row. Generated from the app's own OpenAPI schema by\n`python scripts/make_postman_per_service.py` \u2014 re-run it after changing\nroutes rather than editing requests by hand.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Materials",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Adjust Lot",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/materials/lots/{{lot_id}}/adjust",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "materials",
                "lots",
                "{{lot_id}}",
                "adjust"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "lot_id",
                  "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "A COUNTED STOCK CORRECTION: +/- delta, with a reason, audited.\n\nThe honest form of \"edit the quantity\" \u2014 it records a MOVEMENT rather than\noverwriting the number, so the ledger still adds up and someone can ask a\nyear later why 40 dcm disappeared. Refuses to take stock below what is\nalready reserved for a cut, and refuses to go negative.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"delta\": 0,\n  \"reason\": \"\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create Lot",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/materials/lots",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "materials",
                "lots"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Create a material lot. Registers a child barcode and adds the quantity to\nstock in one transaction.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"category\": \"\",\n  \"subtype\": \"\",\n  \"article\": \"\",\n  \"colour\": \"\",\n  \"attributes\": {},\n  \"supplier_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"sheets\": [\n    {\n      \"dcm\": 0,\n      \"note\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Lot",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/materials/lots/{{lot_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "materials",
                "lots",
                "{{lot_id}}"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "lot_id",
                  "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "One lot: identity, its three stock numbers, its barcode, and which of its\nfields the edit form may show."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Leather By Style",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/materials/leather-by-style",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "materials",
                "leather-by-style"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "style_id",
                  "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "50",
                  "description": "Rows to return (1-200).",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "offset",
                  "value": "0",
                  "description": "Rows to skip before returning `limit` rows.",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Arrived / consumed / available per style \u2014 #19.\n\nAll three come from places that already record them, which is why this is a\nread and not a new ledger. The consumed figure is split by rework (#3), so\n\"this style cost X, of which Y was defects\" is answerable."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List Lots",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/materials/lots",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "materials",
                "lots"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "category",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "LEATHER | LINING | ACCESSORY",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "subtype",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "article",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "colour",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "thickness",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "size",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "sku_id",
                  "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
                  "description": "Pre-select the lot this SKU was last cut from.",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "required",
                  "value": "0",
                  "description": "Total qty this cut needs; flags lots that cover it.",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "THE LOT PICKER for the cut screen \u2014 filter down to the lot, get its id.\n\nThis is the endpoint that lets a frontend supply `leather_lot_id` /\n`lining_lot_id` to `POST /production/log`. The other two material GETs\ncannot: `/materials/spec` returns the FORM DEFINITION (which boxes to\nrender), and `/materials/stock` returns AGGREGATE TOTALS with the lot ids\nsummed away.\n\nTypical cut-screen flow:\n    GET /materials/lots?category=LEATHER&sku_id=<sku>\n      \u2192 `options` fills the article / colour / thickness dropdowns\n      \u2192 the row with `last_used_for_sku: true` is pre-selected\n    \u2026narrow with &article=&colour=&thickness= as the user picks\n      \u2192 one row (material is one lot per spec), take its `lot_id`\n    POST /production/log with consumption.leather_lot_id + dcm\n\nPass `required` (dcm per piece \u00d7 piece count) and each lot reports\n`covers_required`, so a lot that cannot cover the batch can be greyed out\nBEFORE the cut instead of warning after it.\n\nExhausted lots are returned, not hidden \u2014 a manager searching for a lot they\nknow exists must find it, with `available: 0` explaining itself."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Lot History",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/materials/lots/{{lot_id}}/history",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "materials",
                "lots",
                "{{lot_id}}",
                "history"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "lot_id",
                  "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every delivery of this lot, newest first \u2014 the purchase history (#16).\n\nDeclared BEFORE /lots/{lot_id} so the literal path segment wins: FastAPI\nmatches in declaration order, and the bare route would otherwise swallow\n\"history\" as a lot id and 422 on the UUID parse."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Material Spec",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/materials/spec",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "materials",
                "spec"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "category",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "LEATHER | LINING | ACCESSORY",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "subtype",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "RIBS/KNIT ; BUTTON/ZIP/THREAD/OTHER",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "The fields to SHOW for a category: which to filter stock by, which are\nrequired to add a lot, and the quantity field + unit. Drives the Add-New form\nand the stock search boxes so the UI matches the material class exactly."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Piece Consumption",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/materials/pieces/{{piece_id}}/consumption",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "materials",
                "pieces",
                "{{piece_id}}",
                "consumption"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "piece_id",
                  "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "What ONE garment took, hide by hide \u2014 #17 / #28.\n\nA piece cut through the new grid lists its actual sheets. One cut the old way\n(a typed dcm) lists none, which is the honest answer: nobody recorded which\nhides those were."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Receive",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/materials/receive",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "materials",
                "receive"
              ]
            },
            "description": "approved adds to stock; a PO-mismatch is rejected (409) unless a DM/MD\nsends approve_mismatch=true, which receives it into a new substitute lot.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"lot_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"supplier_order_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"approved_qty\": 0,\n  \"rejected_qty\": 0,\n  \"reserve_for_required\": 0,\n  \"approve_mismatch\": false,\n  \"sheets\": [\n    {\n      \"dcm\": 0,\n      \"note\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Record Manual Issue",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/materials/issues",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "materials",
                "issues"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Record a material issued to one garment OUTSIDE its spec. Spends stock.\n\nTHE ESCAPE HATCH THAT MAKES THE FROZEN RECIPE ACCEPTABLE. A released style's\nspec cannot be edited \u2014 its garments are already being issued against it \u2014 so\na wrong article is corrected by recording what was ACTUALLY handed over, not\nby rewriting the recipe underneath live pieces.\n\nRepeatable on purpose: three corrections on one garment are three real\nevents, and none of them makes the kit checklist think a spec line was\nsatisfied.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"piece_barcode\": \"\",\n  \"piece_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"material_lot_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"lot_barcode\": \"\",\n  \"employee_barcode\": \"\",\n  \"employee_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"qty\": 0,\n  \"note\": \"\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Retire Lot",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/materials/lots/{{lot_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "materials",
                "lots",
                "{{lot_id}}"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "lot_id",
                  "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "RETIRE a lot \u2014 deactivate it and retire its barcode. Never a hard delete.\n\nPresent it as \"retire\", not \"delete\". Cut events point at this lot and are\nthe consumption history the costing and traceability screens are built on;\nthe row and every event survive. A scan of the old label returns 410 Gone\n(\"this lot was retired\"), not 404 (\"invalid barcode\").\n\n409 while any stock is still reserved for a cut."
          },
          "response": []
